  *   X qpc seq               the FIFO walker reached flip `seq`: translated
- *   P qpc seq frame pc      Present() of flip `seq` returned (pc = DXGI present count)
- *   D qpc pc sync_qpc       DXGI frame statistics: present `pc` reached the display
- *                           at the vblank stamped sync_qpc
+ *   P qpc seq frame pc hr   Present() of flip `seq` returned (pc = DXGI present count,
+ *                           hr = signed HRESULT; only 0/S_OK eligible for display).
+ *   D qpc pc present_refresh sync_refresh sync_qpc
+ *                           DXGI displayed present and refresh reference. Display
+ *                           QPC = sync_qpc + (present_refresh-sync_refresh)*period;
+ *                           sync_qpc alone is NOT the present's display time.
+ *                           D is suppressed for non-S_OK presents; match pc to
+ *                           its successful P event before accepting a sample.
  *   C qpc vblank period     DWM composition clock (last display vblank, period)
  *   N qpc frame run ...     netplay boundary (src/netplay), K.. other notes
+ *   # trace_dropped=N       cumulative bounded-queue overflow; trace incomplete
  *
  * PS3_LATENCY_WATCH=addr:len[,addr:len...] (hex): guest bytes printed with
  * every F line as big-endian 32-bit words. PS3_LATENCY_DUMP=addr:len appends
  * those bytes per flip to <log>.dump (u32 seq, i64 qpc, bytes) for finding
  * which words to watch.
  *
- * Off (no PS3_LATENCY_LOG) every call is one predictable branch.
+ * Text timing events use a bounded asynchronous disk writer (50 ms flush).
+ * PS3_LATENCY_SYNC=1 restores foreground text writes/flushes for A/B tests.
+ * PS3_LATENCY_DUMP is an intrusive synchronous guest-memory diagnostic; omit
+ * it for frame-pacing measurements. Off, every call is one predictable branch.
  */
 #ifndef PS3RECOMP_LAT_LOG_H
 #define PS3RECOMP_LAT_LOG_H
